# Findings reviewed and knowingly accepted. Every entry names its drop
# condition; the weekly supply-chain sweep is the review point. No bare
# catch-alls — the gate stays actionable for anything not listed here.

# util-linux / libblkid integer overflow (HIGH). Fixed in Debian trixie as
# 2.41.5-0+deb13u1, but no python:3.14-slim rebuild carries the fix yet and
# the base digest is pinned. The container never parses block-device
# partition tables, so the libblkid path is unreachable here.
# Added: 2026-08-17. Drop when: a python:3.14-slim digest bump clears it
# (dependabot tracks the slim tag and will open the PR).
CVE-2026-53615

# msgpack 1.1.2 vendored inside pip (GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964, HIGH): unpacker
# out-of-bounds read on untrusted data. The image's only pip runs happen at
# build time, against the hash-pinned requirements.lock and the
# checksum-verified wheel — pip never unpacks untrusted msgpack in the
# running container.
# Added: 2026-08-17. Drop when: the base ships pip with vendored
# msgpack >= 1.2.1.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# setuptools 70.3.0 bundled in the base image (CVE-2025-47273, HIGH):
# PackageIndex path traversal. setuptools is never invoked at runtime —
# PID 1 is `alle run`; nothing imports it or shells out to it.
# Added: 2026-08-17. Drop when: the base ships setuptools >= 78.1.1 or
# stops bundling it.
CVE-2025-47273
